cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, please cite it as below and link to the page on themomsite.com that the figure comes from."
type: dataset
title: "The Mom Site open data: pregnancy and family benefits by state, and the US doula workforce"
authors:
  - name: "The Mom Site editorial team"
    website: "https://themomsite.com/about/"
abstract: >-
  State-by-state data for all 50 states and DC on Medicaid and CHIP for pregnancy,
  WIC, paid family and medical leave, Medicaid coverage of doulas and lactation
  consultants, breast pumps, child care assistance, county childcare prices and
  child car seat laws, each fact tied to a cited source. Also the doula workforce
  counts behind "The US doula workforce in 2026" (23,197 active doula NPIs in the
  September 2026 NPPES file, by state and by year issued).
